9
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
They Shall Not Grow Old is a 2018 documentary film
directed and produced by Peter Jackson.

10
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
It was created using footage of the First World War held by the British Imperial War Museum (IWM), most of which
was previously unseen, and all of which was over 100 years old by the time of the film's release.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Much of the footage was colourised and restored using modern production techniques for its use in
the film, and sound effects and voice acting were added to the silent footage.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
The film's narration was edited from interviews with British WWI
veterans from the collections of the BBC and the IWM.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
Jackson dedicated the film—his first documentary as
director—to his grandfather, who fought in WWI.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
He said his intention was for the film to be an immersive experience of "what it was
like to be a soldier", rather than a story or recounting of events.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
The crew reviewed 100 hours of archival film footage and 600 hours of interviews with
200 WWI veterans to find the materials from which to construct the film.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The film's title was inspired by a line ("They shall grow not old, as we that are left grow old") from
Laurence Binyon's 1914 poem "For the Fallen", famous for being used in the "Ode of Remembrance".

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
The film premiered simultaneously at the BFI London Film Festival and in selected cinemas in the UK on 16 October 2018,
before airing on BBC Two on 11 November, the hundredth anniversary of the Armistice of 11 November 1918.

18
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
In the US, following the success of screenings of the film by
Fathom Events on 17 and 27 December, Warner Bros.

19
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
Pictures gave the film a wide theatrical release in February 2019.

20
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
Critics acclaimed the film for its restoration work,
immersive atmosphere, and portrayal of war.

21
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:36,000
The film explores themes of world war i, trenches,
1910s, trench warfare, armistice day.
